Another Claude session sent a message:
<teammate-message teammate_id="cascade-correctness-fix" color="green" summary="Final report: both cascade.rs bugs fixed, tests+clippy pass">
Both bugs fixed in crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs. TDD followed throughout (failing test confirmed first, then minimal fix, then passing).

## Bug 1: Linked-group version convergence

Location: `solve_cascade`'s "// Spec §G.6.7" block, ~line 286.

Exact change — replaced the per-member independent `bump_target` call with a two-pass convergence:

```rust
if max_sev > Severity::None {
    for id in &member_ids {
        let cur_sev = out.severities.get(id).copied().unwrap_or(Severity::None);
        if max_sev > cur_sev {
            out.severities.insert(id.clone(), max_sev);
        }
    }

    let mut winner: Option<Version> = None;
    for id in &member_ids {
        let candidate = bump_target(id, max_sev, &input)?;
        winner = Some(match winner {
            None => candidate,
            Some(best) => {
                let cmp = Version::compare(&candidate, &best).map_err(
                    |_grammar_mismatch| GraphError::GroupGrammarMismatch {
                        group: g.name.clone(),
                        members: member_ids
                            .iter()
                            .filter_map(|m| out.targets.get(m).map(|v| (m.clone(), v.clone())))
                            .collect(),
                    },
                )?;
                if cmp.is_gt() { candidate } else { best }
            }
        });
    }
    let winner = winner.expect("linked group has at least one member");

    for id in member_ids {
        if out.targets.get(&id) != Some(&winner) {
            out.targets.insert(id.clone(), winner.clone());
            out.reasons.insert(id.clone(), BumpReason::LinkedGroupUnion { group: g.name.clone() });
            worklist.insert(id.clone());
            changed = true;
        }
    }
}
```

Severities are raised first for all below-`max_sev` members, then every member's candidate target at `max_sev` is computed and the max (via `Version::compare`, erroring to `GraphError::GroupGrammarMismatch` on a grammar clash) is assigned to *every* member, even ones already sitting at what looked like the right severity — matching spec §G.6.7's `winner ← max over pairs' versions`.

New unit test `test_linked_group_converges_target_version_across_divergent_bases` (pkg-a base `1.4.0`, pkg-b base `2.7.3`, seed pkg-a Minor):
- **Before fix**: `assertion left == right failed / left: Version{... "1.5.0" ...} / right: Version{... "2.8.0" ...}` — pkg-a stuck on its own independently-computed target instead of converging.
- **After fix**: passes; both targets `2.8.0`.

Side effect (outside the stated cascade.rs-only scope, flagging explicitly): two pre-existing integration tests in `crates/callisto-graph/tests/graph_tests.rs` were asserting the *old buggy* diverging-version behavior (`test_linked_group_maintains_independent_versions` expected `1.0.1`/`2.0.1` instead of converged `2.0.1`/`2.0.1`; `test_linked_group_version_convergence` expected `1.5.0`/`2.8.0` instead of converged `2.8.0`/`2.8.0`). I corrected both assertions to the spec-correct converged values and renamed the first to `test_linked_group_converges_shared_version` since its old name now described the opposite of what it tests. Let me know if you'd rather I revert the rename/expectations and leave those as a separate follow-up.

## Bug 2: Pre-release pinned baseline

Location: `bump_target`, ~line 344.

Exact change:
```rust
let versioning = callisto_format::SemVerVersioning;

if let Some(pre) = input.pre {
    let pinned_base = pre.initial_versions.get(id.name()).unwrap_or(&base);
    versioning
        .bump_prerelease(pinned_base, sev, &pre.tag, &base)
        .map_err(GraphError::Bump)
} else {
    versioning.bump(&base, sev).map_err(GraphError::Bump)
}
```

