  {
    key: 'graph-core',
    label: 'callisto-graph core',
    prompt: 'You are an adversarial code reviewer. Read ALL of: /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/aggregate.rs (1382 lines, primary target), cascade.rs (~832 lines), walk.rs, lib.rs, and tests/cascade_tests.rs. Also skim docs/01-spec.md for spec context on cascade behavior.\n\nEvaluate for ALL of:\n\n1. BUGS: aggregate.rs since-resolution - does it use gix or still shell out (should use GitRepository::resolve_commit), cascade.rs linked-group convergence - does the worklist correctly re-enqueue dependents, cycle detection in dependency graph, PackageId::matches cross-ecosystem ambiguity (bare name matching both Cargo and npm for same name), version baseline when no tag exists (fresh repo), walk deduplication\n2. PERFORMANCE: aggregate.rs is a god object at 1382 lines - identify hot paths, O(n^2) graph traversal, HashMap where BTreeMap needed for deterministic output\n3. SPEC GAPS: multi-ecosystem packages (Cargo + npm wrapper in same directory), root vs leaf package modeling\n4. CODE ORGANIZATION: aggregate.rs at 1382 lines - identify 3-4 logical clusters for separate modules, functions >60 lines in aggregate.rs (list all), cascade.rs at 832 lines - same, what belongs in lib.rs vs aggregate.rs\n5. MISSING EDGE CASES: empty workspace, single package workspace, circular dependency A->B->A, package with no commits since last tag\n6. ERROR HANDLING: .unwrap() in non-test code\n\nProduce at least 12 findings. Return JSON.'
