  },
  {
    key: 'vcs-conventional-changelog',
    label: 'callisto-vcs + callisto-conventional + callisto-changelog',
    prompt: 'You are an adversarial code reviewer. Read ALL of: /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-vcs/src/lib.rs (~1099 lines), src/shell.rs (~525 lines), any other vcs src files, /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-conventional/src/ (all files), /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-changelog/src/ (all files).\n\nEvaluate for ALL of:\n\n1. BUGS: commits_since_with_pathspec was just fixed with HashSet exclusion - does commits_since() (without pathspecs) have the same branchy-history bug with break-on-SHA? Tags on merge commits - does the revwalk handle them? Shallow clones - what happens when git history is shallow? Conventional commit BREAKING CHANGE footer detection - is it detected in both footer AND body? Multi-paragraph footers? Scoped commits (feat(parser): ...)? changelog ordering (newest first)?\n2. PERFORMANCE: HashSet-based exclusion does a full revwalk from since - for deep histories is this efficient? Is there a depth limit option? Dead code in vcs/lib.rs from pre-refactor?\n3. SPEC GAPS: empty changelog sections (no fixes in this release)? Changelog template matching docs/01-spec.md?\n4. CODE ORGANIZATION: callisto-vcs/lib.rs at 1099 lines - identify natural split points (GitRepository methods vs commit iteration vs tag operations), shell.rs at 525 lines, logic in callisto-conventional that belongs in callisto-vcs\n5. MISSING EDGE CASES: empty repo (HEAD has no commits), commit with no author/email, commit message that is only whitespace, tag pointing to a tree not a commit\n6. ERROR HANDLING: .unwrap() in non-test code\n\nProduce at least 10 findings. Return JSON.'
  },
  {
    key: 'moon-cli',
    label: 'callisto-moon + callisto-cli',
    prompt: 'You are an adversarial code reviewer. Read ALL of: /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-moon/src/ (all files), crates/callisto-moon/tests/moon_wasm_sandbox.rs (~955 lines), crates/callisto-cli/src/ (all files including commands/*.rs), crates/callisto-cli/tests/ (all files), .github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml.\n\nEvaluate for ALL of:\n\n1. BUGS: callisto-moon/locator.rs MoonProjectGraph schema was just fixed to use data HashMap - verify declared_edges() correctly resolves dependency IDs when both from and to projects exist in data, does the WASM extension correctly implement the full moon PDK handshake (register_extension/execute_extension/initialize_extension returning correct types), CLI subcommand wiring (are all spec-required subcommands implemented), does callisto publish command exist and correctly call PublishOrchestrator, CLI error messages (raw Rust errors leaked to user vs user-friendly messages)\n2. PERFORMANCE: MoonProjectLocator OnceLock caching correct?\n3. SPEC GAPS: CLI flags in docs/01-spec.md that are missing from implementation, moon extension operations the spec requires but are not exposed\n4. CODE ORGANIZATION: callisto-cli/commands/add.rs at 425 lines (too large?), moon_wasm_sandbox.rs at 955 lines (should be split?), logic in callisto-cli that belongs in callisto-graph\n5. MISSING EDGE CASES: callisto run in non-workspace-root directory, workspace with no packages, missing moon binary\n6. ERROR HANDLING: .unwrap() in non-test CLI code, errors with context (which file, which package)\n\nProduce at least 10 findings. Return JSON.'
