{
  "executive_summary": "I verified the top-severity claims against source rather than trusting the scan agents. 84 raw findings dedupe to ~62 distinct issues; the scan agents' severity labels were roughly calibrated but three \"medium\" findings are actually release-corrupting P0s and about a dozen \"high/medium\" findings are cosmetic.\n\nThe through-line of every genuinely dangerous finding is the same failure mode: **a value is captured in a plan or config and then silently discarded at an execution boundary.** `NpmPublish::tag` is set to \"next\" for prereleases and never passed to `npm publish` (prereleases land on `latest`). `PypiPublish::index` and `CratePublish::registry` are stored and never reach `twine`/`cargo` (private packages publish to the PUBLIC registry). `aggregate()`'s `_pre` parameter is underscore-discarded, so changesets are marked consumed during a `pre` cycle. `update_dependency_spec` in python.rs returns `Ok(())` when the dep is not found, and `update_optional_dependencies` is a bare `Ok(())` no-op. `action.yml` writes `published=true` to GITHUB_OUTPUT before the publish command runs. The config policy lookup in aggregate.rs uses `==` where the rest of the codebase uses `matches()`, so bare-name `[[package]]` rules are silently inert.\n\nConfirmed by direct read: publish_client.rs:117-128 hardcodes `--access public` with no `--tag`; publish_client.rs:149-164 builds the twine invocation with no `--repository-url`; aggregate.rs:172 `_pre` has zero use sites and aggregate.rs:216 uses `id == &pkg.id`; python.rs:283-371 has the silent-Ok path and ignores `_kind`; python.rs:380-386 is the no-op; action.yml:80-84 collapses exit 1 and exit 2 into `HAS_CHANGESETS=false`; moon_wasm_sandbox.rs:329 emits `{\"projects\":[...]}` while locator.rs:64-66 requires `{\"data\":{...}}`.\n\nThat last one is a live CI break, not a latent bug \u2014 five tests in moon_wasm_sandbox.rs assert `exit_code == 0` and will fail deserialization today. It is 20 minutes of work and should go first regardless of everything else.\n\nDowngrades I am making against the scanners: `is_bare_semver` accepting `1.2.3+build` (F-15) is benign \u2014 round_trip replaces the requirement wholesale, so \"losing\" build metadata on a spec being overwritten is the intended behavior. npm's `detect_fingerprint` has_bom (F-13) is dead-but-corrected by the caller. The dead `Severity::None` arms (F10) and the model derive/doc-comment findings are style. The workspace `unwrap_used = \"allow\"` finding is correct in principle but flipping it to `warn` would produce hundreds of call-site churn diffs across every crate \u2014 that is a separate campaign, not an audit fix, and I am deferring it.\n\nNote on collisions: agents `fix-bom-crlf` and `fix-manifest-cache` are live in this session and own cargo.rs. Track T07 must coordinate or land after them.",
